e ? $event->data[0] : $event->result; \n```\n\nBefore this line the array is:\n\n```\nArray\n(\n[conditions] => Array\n(\n[Group.place_id] => 82\n[Group.deleted] => 0\n)\n[fields] =>\n[joins] => Array\n(\n)\n[limit] => 20\n[offset] =>\n[order] => Array\n(\n[0] =>\n)\n[page] => 1\n[group] =>\n[callbacks] => 1\n[maxLimit] => 100\n[paramType] => named\n) \n```\n\nand after this line it is:\n\n```\nArray\n(\n[conditions] => Array\n(\n[Group.deleted != ] => 1\n)\n[fields] =>\n[joins] => Array\n(\n)\n[limit] => 20\n[offset] =>\n[order] => Array\n(\n[0] =>\n)\n[page] => 1\n[group] =>\n[callbacks] => 1\n[maxLimit] => 100\n[paramType] => named\n) \n```\n\nI'm using the CakeDC search plugin but it also happens when I run a search from the console that is via a shell.\n\nHere's another example, this is my query:\n$places = $this->Place->find('all', array('conditions' => array('Place.id' => 1), 'fields' => array('Place.id', 'Place.shortname')));\n\nConsole output after $this->result has been processed:\nArray\n(\n    [conditions] => Array\n        (\n            [Place.deleted != ] => 1\n        )\n\n```\n[fields] => Array\n    (\n        [0] => Place.id\n        [1] => Place.shortname\n    )\n\n[joins] => Array\n    (\n    )\n\n[limit] => 4\n[offset] => \n[order] => Array\n    (\n        [0] => Array\n            (\n                [0] => Place.shortname\n            )\n\n    )\n\n[page] => 1\n[group] => \n[callbacks] => 1\n[recursive] => -1\n```\n\n)\n\nAny ideas as to why my criteria is being removed?\n","closed_by":{"login":"zen-nomind","id":5120778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxMjA3Nzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5120778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zen-nomind","html_url":"https://github.com/zen-nomind","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zen-nomind/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zen-nomind/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zen-nomind/gists{/gist_id}","star